pve-ups-panel (2.1.5) stable; urgency=high

  * pve-ups-notify: run via sudo so it executes as root when invoked by
    upsmon (which drops privileges to the nut user). Add
    /etc/sudoers.d/pve-ups-panel granting nut NOPASSWD access to the
    notify hook only, with env_keep for NOTIFYTYPE and UPSNAME. This
    fixes notifications and event log writes being silently dropped.
  * pve-ups-notify: add NOTIFYTYPE whitelist (10 valid NUT events) and
    sanitise UPSNAME to [A-Za-z0-9_@.-] to prevent injection when
    running as root.
  * Notify.pm: remove OVERLOAD from %NUT_EVENTS — upsmon does not
    accept it as a NOTIFYFLAG type, causing a startup warning.
  * Notify.pm: fix service name nut-client → nut-monitor when restarting
    upsmon after saving notification settings (nut-client is a package
    name, not a systemd service; the correct service is nut-monitor).
  * debian/control: add sudo to Depends.
  * postinst: create /etc/sudoers.d/pve-ups-panel (0440) and
    /var/log/pve-ups-panel/ on install.
  * prerm: remove /etc/sudoers.d/pve-ups-panel on uninstall.

 -- YoMin Su <aaaa1234567891016@gmail.com>  Thu, 29 May 2026 14:00:00 +0800

pve-ups-panel (2.1.4) stable; urgency=low

  * Notifications: fix saved targets/enabled/threshold silently discarded
    on reload. _loadData used Ext.apply(obj, def, savedValues) where the
    third argument is only applied when the property is absent — meaning
    stored values were always overridden by built-in defaults. Replaced
    with Object.assign({}, def, savedOverrides) so saved state is
    correctly restored.
  * Shutdown Rules, Notifications: display Ext.toast('Settings saved.')
    on successful PUT so users receive immediate visual confirmation
    instead of a silent data reload.
  * History: enable auto-refresh via RRDStore startUpdate/stopUpdate
    (interval 60 s). Charts now update automatically while the tab is
    active and stop polling when the user navigates away.

 -- YoMin Su <aaaa1234567891016@gmail.com>  Thu, 29 May 2026 08:00:00 +0800

pve-ups-panel (2.1.3) stable; urgency=low

  * Convert RRD collector from timer+oneshot to persistent daemon.
    Eliminates ~1440 journal entries/day caused by repeated start/stop
    cycles. pve-ups-rrd-collect now runs as Type=simple with an internal
    epoch-aligned sleep loop (wakes at each wall-clock :00 second),
    matching RRD step boundaries without drift. SIGTERM exits cleanly.
    pve-ups-panel-rrdcollect.timer removed; service depends on
    multi-user.target instead of timers.target.

 -- YoMin Su <aaaa1234567891016@gmail.com>  Thu, 29 May 2026 04:00:00 +0800

pve-ups-panel (2.1.2) stable; urgency=low

  * pve-ups-panel.js: fix UPS tab not restored after page refresh.
    Switch injection point from PVE.node.Config.initComponent to
    PVE.panel.Config.insertNodes. PVE's state restoration (findChild +
    menu.setSelection) runs immediately after insertNodes inside
    initComponent; by injecting at insertNodes time our tab is present
    when PVE looks it up, so no second setSelection is required.

